  "narrative": "The enrichment analysis identifies **Eicosanoid Synthesis** (WikiPathways WP167; FDR = 0.0, fold enrichment = 1,112) as the overwhelming top pathway, with five matched compounds: arachidonic acid (C00219), Leukotriene A4 (C00909), 5-HETE (C04805), 15-HETE (C04742), and 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ₂ (C14717). Membership of these compounds in the arachidonic acid metabolism axis is independently confirmed by the pathway-membership lookup across KEGG, SMPDB, and Reactome databases.\n\n**Key driver compounds.** Arachidonic acid (C00219) serves as the central upstream precursor. KEGG graph traversal confirms that arachidonic acid is directly converted to 5-HETE (C04805) via a two-hop route through prostaglandin G₂ (C05356), establishing a forward upstream→downstream relationship. Arachidonic acid is also bidirectionally linked to Leukotriene A4 (C00909) via the same intermediate, placing both the lipoxygenase and prostaglandin branches in a coordinated active state. 15-HETE (C04742) and 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ₂ (C14717) represent downstream lipoxygenase and cyclopentenone prostaglandin products, respectively, consistent with broad activation of the eicosanoid synthesis axis.\n\n**Biological significance.** Coordinated changes across these eicosanoids point to a robust inflammatory or lipid-derived signaling response in the treatment group. HETEs are potent lipid mediators involved in leukocyte chemotaxis and vascular tone regulation; Leukotriene A4 is the precursor to the pro-inflammatory leukotriene C4, and 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ₂ is a cyclopentenone prostaglandin with anti-inflammatory and electrophilic stress-signaling properties. The non-eicosanoid metabolites (N-acetylgalactosamine, 2-ketobutyric acid, glycerol, 4-hydroxybenzoic acid) likely reflect secondary metabolic consequences of the inflammatory cascade—altered energy metabolism, mucin biosynthesis, or oxidative stress responses—but are not the primary drivers of the eicosanoid enrichment signal.",
